  "query_preview": "/Thursday through Monday/...\nThe area will remain under a flattened ridge north of a massive \nPacific high slowly building into the Great Basin region. This \ncontinuous ridging pattern will favor clear skies, dry conditions, \nand the return of warmer than normal temperatures Thursday through \nFriday. A weak shortwave trough passing north of our area late \nFriday may bring in some high cloud coverage, possibly moderating \nthe daytime temperatures on Saturday. Otherwise, broad Pacific \nridging will dominate the region Sunday through early next week, \ncontinuing a much warmer and drier than normal pattern in the \nextended outlook.",
